WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:37.920
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:38.790
Hi.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:42.480
My name is Ani and I'm an
interdisciplinary artist

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.750
practicing at the intersection
of art and science.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.570
I say interdisciplinary
because the mediums of my work

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.700
range from custom
designed circuits

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.940
that mediate your vision,
to the chemical synthesis

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.760
of a perfume that smells
like a particular human,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.190
to biologically engineered
apparatuses that

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.530
control the movement of sperm.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.810
I would say that I'm a
research-based artist,

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.580
and like many
scientists and artists,

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.080
I make work to
understand the world.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.510
At the root of my work,
I think I'm constantly

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:13.690
trying to ask, how do
scientific theories inform

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:16.470
culture, subjectivity, and
what it means to be human?

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.610
Hi, my name is Angel.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:24.460
I'm a graduating student in
the program for Art, Culture

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.410
and Technology.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:29.080
My work at MIT has
been about looking

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.080
at science and technology
from the point-of-view

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.270
of a critical art
practice, asking

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:38.350
questions of what it produces
beyond practical empirical

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:39.400
knowledge.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.750
And so my projects have engaged
with the mindsets, the space,

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:47.710
the images, and the materiality
that the science and technology

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:48.745
infrastructure produces.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:52.740
Hello.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.620
My name is Jessica
Sarah Rinland.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:02:00.330
My work investigates and unifies
opposing themes, interweaving

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:03.390
original and found
material, highlighting

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:06.570
the incongruity of
factual accounts.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:10.180
My core interest lies in the
fluctuation of knowledge,

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.900
how facts, and the way
they are disseminated,

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.540
develop and change
over time, and how

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.580
this affects
human's relationship

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.000
with and within nature.

